            <ArticleTitle>[Incidental detection of a rare liver tumor: angiomyolipoma].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>847-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the case of a woman who presented a single liver lesion with no evidence of specific findings at Doppler US, CT, nuclear studies and MRI to suggest angiomyolipoma. The final diagnosis was confirmed at anatomopathology and immunohistochemistry which demonstrated positive anti-HMB 45 aspect.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
